return [
    'Getting Started' => [

        'System overview' => [
            'body' => '<p>The MAIIC IFRS 9 platform is the single system in which the corporation measures Expected Credit Loss (ECL, the provision IFRS 9 requires against every loan) and Effective Interest Rate revenue (EIR, the rate that spreads fees and interest evenly over the life of a loan). Every figure on every screen is read from the database for the reporting period you have selected. Nothing is typed in by hand or fixed in the software, and where an input is missing the screen says so rather than showing a zero. The platform is used by credit risk analysts who load data and run the models, by finance staff who review the results, approve what others propose and sign off the month, and by administrators who look after users, periods, settings and maintenance.</p>'
                . '<h4>What you see on the screen</h4><p>The dark green sidebar on the left lists every part of the platform. Three entries sit at the top and are always shown; below them four blocks, each under its own heading, fold open and closed:</p><ul>'
                . '<li><b>Dashboard</b>: the one-page ECL position for a month, with its trends and charts.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Workspace</b>: the ten-step month-end close checklist, everything awaiting a second person\'s approval, and team messages.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Reports</b>: the report hub. Every report, reconciliation and export (the IFRS 9 reports, the reconciliations, Stress Testing, the RBM return and the auditor pack) opens from it.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Data foundation</b>: <b>Portfolio Setup</b> (Loan Portfolios, Product Groups, Sector Types), <b>Customer &amp; Loan Data</b> (Clients, Loan Book, Imports &amp; Feeds) and <b>Collateral Management</b> (Collateral Register, Collateral Allocation, Collateral Types).</li>'
                . '<li><b>Financial modelling</b>: <b>EIR &amp; Revenue Recognition</b> (EIR &amp; Revenue Recognition, Restructures &amp; Resets, Accounting Rules, Fee Classification, EIR Calculations, GL Reconciliation), <b>IFRS 9 Model Setup</b> (Staging &amp; SICR Rules, PD Model, LGD Model) and <b>Forward-Looking Information</b> (FLI Month-End, Macro Statistics, Forward-Looking Model, Scenarios &amp; Overlays).</li>'
                . '<li><b>Risk &amp; regulatory</b>: <b>ECL Processing</b> (ECL Calculation, Mega Farm Programme).</li>'
                . '<li><b>Administration &amp; support</b>: <b>Governance</b> (Governance Centre, Audit), <b>Access &amp; Setup</b> (Users &amp; Roles, Financial Periods, Settings) and <b>Support &amp; Maintenance</b> (Support Tickets, Maintenance, System Documentation).</li></ul>'
                . '<p>The next article, Finding your way, explains the sidebar, its icons and how to fold it.</p>'
                . '<h4>The reporting period</h4><p>Almost every screen is scoped to a <b>reporting period</b>, a calendar month written as year and month, for example <code>2025-11</code> (some screens write it <b>Nov 2025</b>). The loan book is built or imported once per month, the models are applied to that month, ECL is calculated for it, and the reports and the Dashboard read it back. When you change the month in a period selector or filter bar, every table, tile and chart on the page is read again from the database. The Dashboard offers only months for which ECL has been calculated; the Workspace offers every month that has a loan book. A month can be locked once its month-end is signed off; nothing then restates it.</p>'
                . '<h4>Roles and second approvals</h4><p>Access is controlled by roles. The built-in administrator role holds every permission. Further roles are made on <b>Users &amp; Roles</b>, <b>Roles &amp; Permissions</b>, by choosing exactly which permissions a role holds. The sidebar shows you only the entries your role may open, and buttons you may not use are hidden; anything refused is explained by a <b>No access rights</b> dialogue. Many changes also need two people (maker-checker): one person proposes, and a different person approves. The person who proposed a change can never approve it.</p>'
                . '<h4>How the work flows</h4><ol><li>Set up portfolios, product groups and sector types (Data foundation, Portfolio Setup).</li><li>Bring in the month: land the E-Banker pack and approve the loan book build, or import a loan book file, on Imports &amp; Feeds; then check the Loan Book.</li><li>Allocate collateral; load the EIR data, classify and review the fees, approve the schedules and lock the EIRs.</li><li>Stage the book, apply the PD and LGD models and run the forward-looking month-end (FLI Month-End).</li><li>Run the ECL Calculation. The month-end job on Maintenance runs these steps in order.</li><li>Review the reports from the Reports hub, approve what waits on the Workspace, Awaiting approval tab, and sign the month off in the Workspace.</li></ol>'
                . '<h4>Common problems</h4><ul><li><b>A page shows no data.</b> Check the reporting period first; most screens open on the latest month that has data.</li><li><b>A menu entry is missing.</b> Your role does not include that permission; ask an administrator.</li><li><b>Approve is greyed out.</b> You proposed the item; a colleague must approve it.</li></ul>',
            'steps' => [
                'Sign in with your email address, password and the security code.',
                'Read the Dashboard for the latest calculated month to see the current position.',
                'Open Workspace to see which close steps are outstanding and what waits for your approval.',
                'Work down the sidebar in the order the work is done: Data foundation, Financial modelling, Risk & regulatory.',
                'Open Reports for every report, reconciliation and export.',
                'Raise anything that needs attention as a Support Ticket under Administration & support, Support & Maintenance.',
            ],
            'images' => ['sidebar-blocks' => 'The sidebar: Dashboard, Workspace and Reports at the top, then the Data foundation, Financial modelling, Risk & regulatory and Administration & support blocks'],
        ],

        'Finding your way: the six working groups' => [
            'body' => '<p>The sidebar on the left is arranged the way the work is done: what comes in, the models that turn it into figures, the regulatory results, and the administration around them. It is now three entries at the top and four foldable blocks below them (the six coloured working groups of earlier releases are gone). Everyone who signs in sees the sidebar, holding only the entries their role may open. This article explains each part, the icons, and how to fold and unfold it.</p>'
                . '<h4>What you see on the screen</h4><ul>'
                . '<li><b>Brand header</b>: the organisation logo (from Settings) and <b>IFRS 9 ECL &amp; EIR Platform</b> in gold. Pressing the logo opens the Dashboard.</li>'
                . '<li><b>The top entries</b>: <b>Dashboard</b> (house icon), <b>Workspace</b> (checklist icon) and <b>Reports</b> (bar-chart icon), their icons in soft gold. They have no heading and are always shown.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Block headings</b>, in small capitals, each with its own icon and colour: <b>Data foundation</b> (stacked layers, sky blue), <b>Financial modelling</b> (linked boxes, green), <b>Risk &amp; regulatory</b> (balance scale, rose) and <b>Administration &amp; support</b> (crossed tools, violet). A chevron at the right points up when the block is open and down when it is folded.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Entries inside a block</b>: plain text hung off a thin guide line in the block\'s colour. A group (for example <b>Customer &amp; Loan Data</b> or <b>Governance</b>) has its own chevron and opens to show its entries one step further in, in smaller text. An entry whose screens are tabs carries a small grey chip with the number of tabs; hover the chip to read their names (for example <b>Imports &amp; Feeds</b> shows 7).</li>'
                . '<li><b>The page you are on</b>: its entry is white on a light tint, and its piece of the guide line becomes a solid bar in the block\'s colour. When its group is folded, the group carries the bar instead.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Collapse menu</b>: a button with a left-pointing chevron at the foot of the sidebar (desktop only).</li></ul>'
                . '<h4>The blocks and what they hold</h4><ul>'
                . '<li><b>Data foundation</b>: <b>Portfolio Setup</b> (tabs Loan Portfolios, Product Groups, Sector Types); <b>Customer &amp; Loan Data</b> with <b>Clients</b>, <b>Loan Book</b> and <b>Imports &amp; Feeds</b> (tabs Imports, E-Banker Loads, Loan Book Builds, Periods Built, Query Register, Take-on Blocks, Take-on Population); <b>Collateral Management</b> (tabs Collateral Register, Collateral Allocation, Collateral Types).</li>'
                . '<li><b>Financial modelling</b>: <b>EIR &amp; Revenue Recognition</b> with <b>EIR Data</b> (tabs Contract Master, Cash Flows, Drawdowns, Reference Rates, Trial Balances, Write-offs, Schedule Review), <b>Restructures &amp; Resets</b>, <b>Accounting Rules</b>, <b>Fee Classification</b>, <b>EIR Calculations</b> (Calculations, Blockers, Coverage by Portfolio, Largest Facilities, EIR as at a Date) and <b>GL Reconciliation</b>; <b>IFRS 9 Model Setup</b> with <b>Staging &amp; SICR Rules</b> (SICR Groups, SICR Alert Items, SICR Trigger Alerts), <b>PD Model</b> (Transition Profiles, Monthly Probability, Cumulative Probability, Internal Grades) and <b>LGD Model</b> (Monthly LGD, Cumulative LGD); <b>Forward-Looking Information</b> with <b>FLI Month-End</b> (Overview, Impact Analysis), <b>Macro Statistics</b> (Dashboard, Variables, Data Entry, Scenario Assumptions, Import / Export), <b>Forward-Looking Model</b> (Credit Loss Data, Correlation Finder, Regression, Model Versions, Adjusted Forecast, Weighted Forecast) and <b>Scenarios &amp; Overlays</b> (Scenario Profiles, Scenario Sets, Economic Scenarios, Manual Overlays, External Calculations, Calculation History).</li>'
                . '<li><b>Risk &amp; regulatory</b>: <b>ECL Processing</b> with <b>ECL Calculation</b> and <b>Mega Farm Programme</b>.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Administration &amp; support</b>: <b>Governance</b> with <b>Governance Centre</b> and <b>Audit</b> (tabs Audit Trail, Audit Trace, Compliance Audits); <b>Access &amp; Setup</b> with <b>Users &amp; Roles</b> (tabs Users, Roles &amp; Permissions), <b>Financial Periods</b> and <b>Settings</b>; <b>Support &amp; Maintenance</b> with <b>Support Tickets</b>, <b>Maintenance</b> and <b>System Documentation</b> (User Manual, Administrator Manual, Technical Manual, Installation Guide).</li></ul>'
                . '<p>The reports are not listed in the sidebar: every report, reconciliation and export opens from the <b>Reports</b> hub, and while you are on one of them the <b>Reports</b> entry stays lit.</p>'
                . '<h4>Buttons and icons</h4><ul>'
                . '<li><b>Block heading</b>: press it to fold or unfold the block. Your choice is remembered for you in this browser. The block that holds the page you open unfolds by itself on every page load.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Group name</b> with its chevron: press it to open or close the group; also remembered for you in this browser. The group holding the current page opens by itself.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Collapse menu</b> (left chevron, hover text <b>Collapse the menu</b>): folds the sidebar to a narrow icon rail and gives the page the width. On the rail the button shows a right chevron, <b>Expand the menu</b>, which opens the full sidebar again. The choice is remembered in this browser.</li>'
                . '<li><b>Icon rail</b>: one icon per top entry and per entry of the blocks: house (Dashboard), checklist (Workspace), bar chart (Reports), database (Portfolio Setup), people (Customer &amp; Loan Data), building (Collateral Management), percent sign (EIR &amp; Revenue Recognition), line chart (IFRS 9 Model Setup), binoculars (Forward-Looking Information), calculator (ECL Processing), shield (Governance), user with a padlock (Access &amp; Setup) and wrench (Support &amp; Maintenance). Thin lines separate the blocks. Hover an icon for its name. The current entry\'s icon turns green with a green bar at its left edge. Pressing an entry opens its page; pressing a group opens the full sidebar with that group open.</li></ul>'
                . '<h4>The breadcrumb</h4><p>Above every page title a breadcrumb gives the page\'s place in the sidebar: block, then group, then entry, then tab, separated by small chevrons, for example <b>Data foundation</b>, <b>Customer &amp; Loan Data</b>, <b>Imports &amp; Feeds</b>, <b>E-Banker Loads</b>. Every crumb but the last is a link: a block or group opens its first entry, a tabbed entry opens its first tab. The last crumb, in green, is the page itself. A detail page adds its own crumbs (for example the record you opened); a page that is not in the sidebar, such as your Profile or a manual, reads <b>Dashboard</b> then its title. The Dashboard itself has no breadcrumb. On a phone the middle crumbs fold into "...".</p>'
                . '<h4>On a phone or narrow window</h4><p>The sidebar is hidden. The three-line button at the left of the top bar (<b>Open sidebar</b>) slides the full sidebar in over a grey backdrop; the white X at its top right (<b>Close sidebar</b>) or a tap on the backdrop closes it. The drawer has no Collapse menu button.</p>'
                . '<h4>Common problems</h4><ul><li><b>An entry I expect is missing.</b> Your role lacks its permission; ask an administrator under Access &amp; Setup, Users &amp; Roles.</li><li><b>A block will not stay folded.</b> It holds the page you are on, and that block opens on every page load.</li><li><b>The sidebar opened folded on another computer.</b> The fold choices are kept in each browser, not on your account.</li><li><b>The rail shows icons with no names.</b> Hover an icon, or press Expand the menu.</li></ul>',
            'steps' => [
                'Press a block heading (Data foundation, Financial modelling, Risk & regulatory, Administration & support) to unfold it.',
                'Press a group name to open it, then press the entry you need; the page you are on is marked with a bar in the block colour.',
                'Use the tabs at the top of the page to move between the screens of one entry.',
                'Read the breadcrumb above the title to see where you are, and press a crumb to go back up.',
